;; demos/scenarios/dense-7500/figures.edn
;;
;; THE ONE PLACE THIS SCENARIO'S MEASURED FIGURES LIVE (author ruling
;; R-figures-file, 2026-09-07; commissioned by ADR-0180's R-gate-gaps).
;; Two documents quote them -- this directory's own README.md, under
;; "What to look for", and docs/consuming-ground-truth.md's Scale table
;; -- and until this file existed they quoted each other, which is how
;; three Scale cells sat at a superseded measurement while nothing went
;; red. `ehrt.docs-tooling.dense-7500-figures-test` now holds both
;; documents equal to this file.
;;
;; TWO HALVES, and the difference between them is exactly what a run
;; can prove.
;;
;; :asserted is REWRITTEN BY bin/demo-exerciser-dense-7500 ON EVERY
;; RUN, between the markers below, from that run's own artefacts. It
;; holds only the figures that script actually generates something to
;; count -- `config.edn` at 7,500 arrivals and at 750. The rewrite is
;; the assertion: a moved count makes the block differ from the
;; committed one, and the script's own tree-clean postcondition fails
;; carrying the diff. Never hand-edit inside the markers.
;;
;; :quoted is HAND-MEASURED and no line of that script touches it. Two
;; kinds of figure live here, for two different reasons. (1) The two
;; sibling configs' counts: the README teaches no command for either,
;; so no run in this tree produces an artefact to count (that README's
;; own note on what is deliberately not checked). (2) Every process
;; wall and peak RSS, for all four cells: a wall is a property of a
;; machine and a load rather than of the corpus, and R-figures-file
;; rules the wall cells dated quotations -- never asserted against a
;; live run. Re-measure them by hand, update :provenance in the same
;; edit, and the gate test then requires both documents to follow.
;;
;; A CELL KEY is `<config file>` and `<arrivals>`, which is how both
;; documents identify a row. `:msg-per-event` is `:messages` over
;; `:events` to four decimal places, and the gate re-derives it rather
;; than trusting it.
{:scenario "dense-7500"
 :seed 20260824
 :flags ["--churn"]

;; BEGIN asserted -- rewritten by bin/demo-exerciser-dense-7500 on every run
 :asserted
 {:config-edn-7500 {:events 167197 :messages 222819 :msg-per-event 1.3327}
  :config-edn-750 {:events 33306}}
;; END asserted

 :quoted
 {:config-edn-7500 {:wall-s 278.64 :peak-rss-mb 2415}
  :config-nobed-7500 {:events 125642 :messages 165466 :msg-per-event 1.3170
                      :wall-s 231.14 :peak-rss-mb 2178}
  :config-bare-7500 {:events 100868 :messages 65457 :msg-per-event 0.6489
                     :wall-s 142.12 :peak-rss-mb 1780}
  :config-edn-750 {:messages 40291 :msg-per-event 1.2097
                   :wall-s 54.37 :peak-rss-mb 1228}}

 :provenance
 {:sha "4ddf62c2"
  :date "2026-09-06"
  :machine "WSL2, 6c/12t i7-10750H, 15 GiB, OpenJDK 21.0.7, JVM defaults as shipped -- MaxHeapSize 3.88 GB, bin/ehrt sets no JVM options"
  :method "one warm-up run, then two timed runs per cell, one JVM per run, a fresh spool target per run, /usr/bin/time -v around each; every figure is the mean of the two timed runs, and both runs of every cell produced the identical event and message counts"}}
